What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/device/link_brightness
What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/device/power_brightness
What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/device/wattmeter_brightness
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	7.4
Contact:	Alexey Charkov <alchark@flipper.net>
Description:	(RW) The Flipper One MCU scales the brightness of each of its
		LED groups by a per-group setting, from 0 (off) to 255 (full).
		The link group holds the RGB LEDs registered by this driver;
		the power and wattmeter groups are driven by the MCU itself.

		The setting applies on top of the brightness and
		multi_intensity of the individual LEDs: those still select a
		colour and level relative to the group setting, and a group
		setting of 0 keeps every LED in the group dark.

		The MCU stores the setting in its flash, so it persists across
		reboots and power cycles, and every write costs a flash write.
		Use the brightness of individual LEDs for anything that changes
		frequently, such as triggers or animations.

		The setting can also be changed from the MCU's own menu, with
		no notification to the host. Reading the file always returns
		the current value from the MCU.

		Format: %u
